WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.541 --> 00:00:01.990
- Oh my God.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.100
I was dying watching your comedy,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.830
you are so funny.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.450
I love when comedians take like,

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.080
real life scenarios that we
all get but no one talks about

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.123
and then you use it like that.

00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:13.260
It's so funny.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.910
- Driving kids back and
forth to school every day,

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.110
you gotta figure out how
you're gonna survive, like.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.380
- Yes, and I try and hang my
hand out, but you're right.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.669
They're never gonna let me in.

00:00:21.669 --> 00:00:22.502
(audience laughs)

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:23.335
They're never gonna, yeah, they're like,

00:00:23.335 --> 00:00:24.168
"I've gotta be somewhere."

00:00:24.168 --> 00:00:25.760
I'm like, don't we all?
- I know.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.130
- But someone told me that
we almost met years ago.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.100
- Oh man, so I was there when you won...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.212
- [Kelly] American Idol?
- American Idol, with my kids.

00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:35.390
(audience claps)
- What?

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.350
Wait, how old were your kids then?

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.390
- So they were little.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.907
You know, they're in
their early twenties now

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.890
but they were little and...
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.350
- So you are the person that...

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.860
you belong to me and
my daughter, and so we-

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.257
- I will cry right now with
that statement, that's so nice.

00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:55.940
- You know, we were going
through, it was a tough time

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.940
and a friend Kevin, who was
a musical director there

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.030
gave me tickets so that
I could take my children

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.530
'cause my daughter loved American idol

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.010
and we got to see you win.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.510
- Oh my gosh!
(audience claps)

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.700
That's a weird full circle moment.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.046
Well awesome, not weird.
- I know.

00:01:14.046 --> 00:01:16.580
- Okay, well let's talk
about your comedy special.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.280
So it's called Fighting
Words, which I love.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.090
Why did you title it that?

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.960
- Well, you know, I took on society

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.290
'cause I'm really, you...

00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:30.730
if you say I don't like
apples on the internet,

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.530
to somebody, that means you hate oranges.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.140
- Yeah, oh you can't say anything.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.600
- No, you can't win for losing.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.480
If you speak up against a cause,
you're inserting yourself.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.410
If you don't, you're ignoring it.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.560
So I was like, you know what?

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.570
I tired of this.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.720
I am going in on everybody.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.462
I don't care where you are.

00:01:47.462 --> 00:01:48.330
- I feel like that's
what comedians do though.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.163
That's what's funny.

00:01:49.163 --> 00:01:50.430
- What we're supposed to do, right?

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:53.557
But everything has gotten so
politicized and I was like,

00:01:53.557 --> 00:01:57.190
"I wanna bring back unity
by making fun of everybody."

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.023
Let's do it, right?
(audience claps)

00:01:58.023 --> 00:01:58.856
- I mean, and that's what I love.

00:01:58.856 --> 00:02:01.489
Comedians, it's like
everyone gets made fun of

00:02:01.489 --> 00:02:04.310
and then everybody gets to
laugh at their own self.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.850
I think, yeah, it's hard though.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.004
I talk about that with friends,

00:02:08.004 --> 00:02:10.077
that we're all on TV and I'm like,

00:02:10.077 --> 00:02:12.677
"Which one of us do you
think will get fired first?"

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.650
I'm like, we get nervous 'cause like,

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.710
it's hard when you're an open person.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.810
and you're also in the
public eye and it's like,

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.840
well I have opinions
too, 'cause I'm a human.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.490
So like, you know, and it's
a hard thing to navigate.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.580
- Well, you know, I just,
I have adopted a belief

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.670
that you can't invalidate
somebody's struggle

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.820
because it doesn't look like your own

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:37.850
and every time I give
myself that, I have peace

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.840
because everybody is looking at life

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:41.850
through their own window

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.350
and we just can't go around
monitor everybody's window.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.330
We have to just say, hopefully
they can come to a place

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.600
where they're reading,
they're seeking information

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.203
and having empathy for
other people, you know?

00:02:54.203 --> 00:02:57.240
Like I think that's... that keeps me sane.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.900
- Yeah, me too.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.140
I think that's a cool thing about art too,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.190
is that we're able to do that through

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:04.740
music, comedy, television, like all of it.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.610
Bombing is hard as a comedian or a singer,

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.290
any kind of entertainer on stage,

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.810
but you figured out a way to
make money off of it, right?

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.643
- Yeah.

00:03:11.643 --> 00:03:12.476
- I love this.

00:03:12.476 --> 00:03:16.750
- So I taped my first comedy show.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.070
Kevin Hart was hosting a
show called One Mic Stand

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.760
and when I walked down the
stairs, this woman yelled out

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.010
at the audience, "who does
this bitch think she is?"

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:32.705
and I proceeded to bomb so
bad 'cause I... it got to me.

00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:33.538
- [Kelly] You let it
get in your head, yeah.

00:03:33.538 --> 00:03:35.280
- And then Kevin Hart handled her later

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.930
but I made a shirt that said,

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.530
Who does this bitch think she is?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.070
And I turned that acronym and now,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.875
bitch stands for being in
total control of herself.

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:50.893
- I love that!
(audience cheering)

00:03:50.893 --> 00:03:52.640
- You need to like, write a book.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.473
- (laughs) I am.

00:03:53.473 --> 00:03:55.010
- Like everything you
keep saying, I'm like,

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.530
gosh, I would read your book.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.091
I love all your little sayings and things.

00:03:58.091 --> 00:03:58.924
- Thank you.

00:03:58.924 --> 00:04:01.660
- And by the way, did it not
occur toy you at one point

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.270
to be like, I'm this bitch.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.980
- I know, it took a while

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.610
- Yeah (laughs) I think I
would go to anger first.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.430
You were nicer, yeah.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.490
- I was broken.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.810
I had bombed!

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.730
I was like, you know, and
then I realized, I was like,

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.720
oh, I gotta work my way to that place

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.820
and when I did I made that shirt

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.300
and then I started selling
'em all over the country

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.370
and just encouraging all women
and saying, you know what?

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.600
Let them question who
you are, just show up.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.790
Just go girl, just do it, do it, do it!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.190
- Isn't it cool how something negative

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.360
ended up being super
positive like in your life?

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.680
I love that.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.980
I love you so much.
- I love you back.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.411
You're so funny and
awesome in person as well.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.410
Aida's special, it's
called Fighting Words.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.737
It's on HBO Max, y'all gotta check it out.

